{"type":"message","id":"6739e2b0","parentId":"2ac0612c","timestamp":"2026-05-21T07:34:59.223Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_LtiUDphzYiApArgwVJWBnEDm","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"./research_payload.json","limit":220}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_dyQk567qf0jINOtEeJNu6b3M","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"./single-topic.json","limit":220}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_fn4B3NXmCcmgXUPB6IHo4q0f","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"./single_topic_news.json","limit":220}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_PO0r8q0sXIPFICfMa90ZV2WR","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"./topic_research.json","limit":220}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","usage":{"input":395,"output":185,"cacheRead":21120,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":21700,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779348895026,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DhsDftmijPCWiQlzDQc1C8ymjhPfq"}}
{"type":"message","id":"1e6f5f7f","parentId":"6739e2b0","timestamp":"2026-05-21T07:34:59.387Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_LtiUDphzYiApArgwVJWBnEDm","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"DeFi United effort to recover KelpDAO exploit funds\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United KelpDAO recovery\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Aave asks Arbitrum to send 30K ETH from Kelp exploiter to ‘DeFi United’\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/arbitrum-dao-asked-to-unfreeze-30k-eth-tied-to-kelp-hacker-direct-them-to-defi-united\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Aave Labs proposed that the Arbitrum DAO unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether tied to the Kelp DAO attack.\",\n    \"The funds are proposed to be directed to 'DeFi United,' a fund aimed at restoring rsETH and compensating its holders.\",\n    \"The Arbitrum Security Council had previously frozen 30,765 Ether (ETH) in a wallet connected to the $293 million Kelp exploit.\",\n    \"The proposal is supported by Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi and Compound.\",\n    \"'DeFi United' has already seen $21 million in contributions from various entities, including Aave Labs CEO Stani Kulechov, Kelp DAO, and others.\",\n    \"An additional $215 million has been pledged by Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi and Lido, subject to governance votes.\",\n    \"Aave was significantly impacted by the exploit, suffering nearly $12 billion in TVL drop and over $190 million in bad debt.\",\n    \"Aave Labs estimates a 49-day timeline for the recovery plan.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether tied to the Kelp DAO attack and to direct those funds to “DeFi United,” a fund aimed at restoring rsETH and compensating its holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council moved to freeze 30,765 Ether (ETH) held in a wallet connected to the $293 million Kelp exploit. In a proposal posted Saturday on the Arbitrum governance forum, Aave Labs said directing those funds to a planned remediation effort would “restore normal conditions for Arbitrum users” and the wider ecosystem and that the Ether on Arbitrum “represents a material contribution” toward restoring the Kelp DAO restaked ETH (rsETH) token. The submission was made with the support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi and Compound, four of the several crypto protocols affected by the hack. The proposal comes days after Aave Labs and others set up the “DeFi United” on Friday in an effort to fully restore the backing of rsETH. Dune Analytics data shows that about $21 million in contributions has already been made, with contributions including those from Aave Labs CEO Stani Kulechov, Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, Golem Foundation, Web3 development platform BGD Labs and Babylon, a Bitcoin-native DeFi protocol. Another $215 million has been pledged by Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi and Lido to assist the recovery effort, which are subject to governance votes. LayerZero, Ethena, Ink Foundation and Frax Finance have also signaled their intention to help. Aave was hit hard by the Kelp DAO exploit, with its total value locked falling nearly $12 billion in a week after the hacker put the stolen rsETH tokens up as collateral on its lending platform to borrow wrapped Ether, leaving more than $190 million in bad debt and triggering a wave of withdrawals. In the Arbitrum proposal, Aave Labs said a full recovery would not only restore rsETH’s backing but also normalize conditions for its holders, liquidity providers and borrowers on Arbitrum and across the broader DeFi ecosystem. Even a “partial recovery would still meaningfully reduce the shortfall,” Aave Labs added. Aave Labs has specifically asked for the 30,765 Ether to be sent to a recovery address controlled by Aave, Kelp DAO and blockchain security platform Certora. Aave Labs said it expects the effort to restore rsETH and compensate its holders to take about 49 days and that it would return the funds if the recovery effort falls through.\"\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779348899387}}
{"type":"message","id":"0c2143bd","parentId":"1e6f5f7f","timestamp":"2026-05-21T07:34:59.387Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_dyQk567qf0jINOtEeJNu6b3M","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Aave-linked DeFi United unveils rsETH recovery plan after $293M Kelp exploit\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United rsETH recovery\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Aave-linked DeFi United unveils rsETH recovery plan after $293M Kelp exploit\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/aave-linked-defi-united-outlines-plan-to-restore-rseth-backing-after-293m-exploit\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/365847/aave-compound-unveil-technical-plan-to-address-fallout-from-290m-kelp-dao-hack\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"The Aave-linked recovery group DeFi United has published a technical implementation plan to restore rsETH backing after the April 18 Kelp bridge exploit released 116,500 rsETH, worth about $293 million at the time, without a corresponding burn on Unichain.\",\n    \"The plan would convert committed Ether (ETH) into rsETH in tranches and deposit the tokens into the affected bridge lockbox, allowing the bridge to resume normal operations once the backing is restored.\",\n    \"DeFi United plans to clear attacker-linked positions across Aave and Compound to recover collateral and resolve market impairments caused by the exploit.\",\n    \"Seven addresses associated with the exploiter still hold active rsETH-backed positions on Aave and Compound, representing about 107,000 rsETH of the original 116,500 rsETH released in the incident.\",\n    \"Consensys and Ethereum co-founder Joe Lubin had joined DeFi United with a commitment of up to 30,000 ETH, while Sharplink, a publicly traded Ethereum treasury company, joined in an advisory role to help structure the recovery plan.\",\n    \"Aave Labs had asked the Arbitrum DAO to release 30,765 ETH frozen by the Arbitrum Security Council after the exploit and send the funds to DeFi United.\",\n    \"As of Tuesday, the DeFi United website showed $302.26 million in total raised or committed toward the recovery effort, equal to 132,706.903 ETH, though some commitments remain subject to DAO votes and final execution.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Aave-Linked DeFi United Details rsETH Recovery Plan\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/aave-linked-defi-united-outlines-plan-to-restore-rseth-backing-after-293m-exploit\\n\\nPublished Time: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 10:54:26 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\nThe Aave-linked recovery group DeFi United has published a technical implementation plan to restore rsETH backing after the April 18 Kelp bridge exploit released 116,500 rsETH, worth about $293 million at the time, without a corresponding burn on Unichain.\\n\\nThe plan would [convert](https://x.com/aave/status/2048958367658332413) committed Ether (ETH) into rsETH in tranches and deposit the tokens into the affected bridge lockbox, allowing the bridge to resume normal operations once the backing is restored. LayerZero and Kelp have also implemented additional security measures before the bridge returns to full operation, according to Aave.\\n\\nIn parallel, DeFi United plans to clear attacker-linked positions across Aave and Compound to recover collateral and resolve market impairments caused by the exploit. The group said seven addresses associated with the exploiter still hold active rsETH-backed positions on Aave and Compound, representing about 107,000 rsETH of the original 116,500 rsETH released in the incident.\\n\\n_**Related:**_[_**Kelp restaking platform exploited, $293M drained in attack**_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/restaking-platform-kelp-exploited-293-million)\\n\\nThe proposed sequence would temporarily adjust the rsETH oracle price to enable controlled liquidations, transfer recovered collateral to a DeFi United multisig, restore the oracle, redeem the rsETH for ETH and use the resulting funds to clear deficits across affected markets.\\n\\nThe recovery plan moves the rsETH effort from pledges and public commitments into a coordinated technical process that depends on governance approvals, temporary oracle changes and execution across several DeFi protocols. While the process is designed to restore rsETH backing, it remains contingent on DAO votes, finalized agreements and the attacker not disrupting the liquidation steps.\\n\\n![Image 1](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=802,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-17.jpeg?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Source:_[_Aave_](https://x.com/aave/status/2048958367658332413)\\n\\n## Ethereum backers joined the recovery effort\\n\\nThe technical plan follows earlier efforts to secure funding and governance support for the rsETH recovery.\\n\\nOn Monday, Consensys and Ethereum co-founder Joe Lubin [had joined DeFi United](https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-backers-commit-up-to-30000-eth-to-rseth-recovery-after-bridge-incident) with a commitment of up to 30,000 ETH, while Sharplink, a publicly traded Ethereum treasury company, joined in an advisory role to help structure the recovery plan.\\n\\n_**Related:**_[_**Crypto protocols pledge 43K ETH to restore rsETH backing**_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/defi-ecosystem-unites-and-pledges-to-rseth-relief-effort)\\n\\nOn the same day, Aave Labs [had asked the Arbitrum DAO](https://cointelegraph.com/news/arbitrum-dao-asked-to-unfreeze-30k-eth-tied-to-kelp-hacker-direct-them-to-defi-united) to release 30,765 ETH frozen by the Arbitrum Security Council [after the exploit](https://cointelegraph.com/news/arbitrum-freezes-71m-ether-connected-kelp-exploit) and send the funds to DeFi United.\\n\\n![Image 2](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-18.jpeg?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_DeFi United secured over $300 million in commitments. Source: DeFi United_\\n\\nAs of Tuesday, the DeFi United website [showed](https://defiunited.world/) $302.26 million in total raised or committed toward the recovery effort, equal to 132,706.903 ETH, though some commitments remain subject to DAO votes and final execution.\\n\\n_**Magazine:**_[_**AI-driven hacks could kill DeFi — unless projects act now**_](https://cointelegraph-magazine.com/exploits-uncovered-by-ai-could-kill-defi-unless-projects-act-now/)\\n\\nCointelegraph is committed to independent, transparent journalism. This news article is produced in accordance with Cointelegraph’s [Editorial Policy](https://cointelegraph.com/editorial-policy) and aims to provide accurate and timely information. Readers are encouraged to verify information independently.\\nTitle: Aave, Compound Unveil Technical Plan to Address Fallout From $290M Kelp DAO Hack\\n\\nURL Source: https://decrypt.co/365847/aave-compound-unveil-technical-plan-to-address-fallout-from-290m-kelp-dao-hack\\n\\nPublished Time: 2026-04-28T17:36:01\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Aave, Compound Unveil Technical Plan to Address Fallout From $290M Kelp DAO Hack - Decrypt\\n\\n[![Image 1: Decrypt logo](https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/full-logo-black.svg)![Image 2: Decrypt logo](https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/full-logo-white.svg)](https://decrypt.co/)[](https://decrypt.co/gg)[](https://decrypt.co/university)[](https://decrypt.co/university)[](https://decrypt.co/emerge)\\n\\n[![Image 3: Decrypt logo](https://img.decrypt.co/insecure/rs:fit:3840:0:0:0/plain/https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/logo-mark-white.svg@webp)![Image 4: Decrypt logo](https://img.decrypt.co/insecure/rs:fit:3840:0:0:0/plain/https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/logo-mark-black.svg@webp)](https://decrypt.co/)\\n\\n[News](https://decrypt.co/news)[Learn](https://decrypt.co/university)[GG](https://decrypt.co/gg)[Emerge](https://decrypt.co/emerge)[Videos](https://decrypt.co/videos)[Newsletters](https://decrypt.co/newsletters)\\n\\nEnglish\\n\\nSign Up[Partner with us](https://dastan.co/partner)\\n\\n* * *\\n\\n* * *\\n\\n[![Image 5: News](blob:http://localhost/0aa0a8ee08caf3bcc8e7e488283150b2)![Image 6: News](blob:http://localhost/9a89213175e2fb47d512c1624a349836)News](https://decrypt.co/news)[![Image 7: Predict](blob:http://localhost/83e225a6c9ce2bac8adf311c3e67de6b)![Image 8: Predict](blob:http://localhost/d3717f8b551ce4e2a9b35e1641d61392)Predict](https://myriad.markets/?utm_source=decrypt&utm_campaign=navbar)[![Image 9: AI](blob:http://localhost/62ceb084dde83843d9887bdc1213ad1f)![Image 10: AI](blob:http://localhost/7aa2f6422d5e2e5af6a262ad86bf9b91)AI](https://decrypt.co/emerge)[![Image 11: Learn](blob:http://localhost/132e5adddd21434e4b62b0d79cacaf2c)![Image 12: Learn](blob:http://localhost/132e5adddd21434e4b62b0d79cacaf2c)Learn](https://decrypt.co/university)[![Image 13: Gaming](blob:http://localhost/e44cea5a102a4ce9cbe1c97f51994f1b)![Image 14: Gaming](blob:http://localhost/f89fd6ac9ca89f35ed6d49f4a70a6652)Gaming](https://decrypt.co/gg)\\n\\n## Coin Prices\\n\\n### [BTC](https://decrypt.co/price/bitcoin)\\n\\n$77,727.00\\n\\n1.54%\\n### [ETH](https://decrypt.co/price/ethereum)\\n\\n$2,341.28\\n\\n2.55%\\n### [XRP](https://decrypt.co/price/xrp)\\n\\n$1.40\\n\\n1.12%\\n### [BNB](https://decrypt.co/price/binance-coin)\\n\\n$628.90\\n\\n0.93%\\n### [USDC](https://decrypt.co/price/usd-coin)\\n\\n$0.999869\\n\\n0.00%\\n### [SOL](https://decrypt.co/price/solana)\\n\\n$85.36\\n\\n1.96%\\n### [TRX](https://decrypt.co/price/tron)\\n\\n$0.323283\\n\\n0.03%\\n### [FIGR_HELOC](https://decrypt.co/price/figure-heloc)\\n\\n$1.033\\n\\n0.29%\\n### [DOGE](https://decrypt.co/price/dogecoin)\\n\\n$0.109735\\n\\n10.44%\\n### [WBT](https://decrypt.co/price/whitebit)\\n\\n$55.07\\n\\n1.66%\\n### [USDS](https://decrypt.co/price/usds)\\n\\n$0.999764\\n\\n-0.01%\\n### [HYPE](https://decrypt.co/price/hyperliquid)\\n\\n$40.62\\n\\n0.81%\\n### [LEO](https://decrypt.co/price/bitfinex)\\n\\n$10.36\\n\\n-0.03%\\n### [ADA](https://decrypt.co/price/cardano)\\n\\n$0.253118\\n\\n2.82%\\n### [BCH](https://decrypt.co/price/bitcoin-cash)\\n\\n$455.07\\n\\n1.72%\\n### [XMR](https://decrypt.co/price/monero)\\n\\n$382.36\\n\\n1.02%\\n### [LINK](https://decrypt.co/price/chainlink)\\n\\n$9.40\\n\\n1.76%\\n### [CC](https://decrypt.co/price/canton-network)\\n\\n$0.150786\\n\\n1.15%\\n### [ZEC](https://decrypt.co/price/zcash)\\n\\n$334.99\\n\\n-0.35%\\n### [XLM](https://decrypt.co/price/stellar)\\n\\n$0.164259\\n\\n0.33%\\n### [M](https://decrypt.co/price/memecore)\\n\\n$3.55\\n\\n1.27%\\n### [USD1](https://decrypt.co/price/usd1-wlfi)\\n\\n$0.999547\\n\\n-0.04%\\n### [LTC](https://decrypt.co/price/litecoin)\\n\\n$57.56\\n\\n4.38%\\n### [AVAX](https://decrypt.co/price/avalanche)\\n\\n$9.42\\n\\n2.74%\\n### [HBAR](https://decrypt.co/price/hedera-hashgraph)\\n\\n$0.090681\\n\\n2.00%\\n### [SHIB](https://decrypt.co/price/shiba-inu)\\n\\n$0.00000651\\n\\n6.32%\\n### [USDE](https://decrypt.co/price/ethena-usde)\\n\\n$0.999229\\n\\n0.01%\\n### [SUI](https://decrypt.co/price/sui)\\n\\n$0.936234\\n\\n1.26%\\n### [RAIN](https://decrypt.co/price/rain)\\n\\n$0.00745332\\n\\n1.39%\\n### [PYUSD](https://decrypt.co/price/paypal-usd)\\n\\n$0.999983\\n\\n0.00%\\n### [TON](https://decrypt.co/price/the-open-network)\\n\\n$1.32\\n\\n1.48%\\n### [CRO](https://decrypt.co/price/crypto-com)\\n\\n$0.069339\\n\\n0.09%\\n### [USYC](https://decrypt.co/price/hashnote-usyc)\\n\\n$1.12\\n\\n-0.00%\\n### [XAUT](https://decrypt.co/price/tether-gold)\\n\\n$4,561.39\\n\\n-0.97%\\n### [TAO](https://decrypt.co/price/bittensor)\\n\\n$261.44\\n\\n5.16%\\n### [USDG](https://decrypt.co/price/global-dollar)\\n\\n$0.999782\\n\\n0.00%\\n### [WLFI](https://decrypt.co/price/world-liberty-financial)\\n\\n$0.07344\\n\\n0.47%\\n### [BUIDL](https://decrypt.co/price/blackrock-usd-institutional-digital-liquidity-fund)\\n\\n$1.00\\n\\n0.00%\\n### [PAXG](https://decrypt.co/price/pax-gold)\\n\\n$4,556.28\\n\\n-1.04%\\n### [MNT](https://decrypt.co/price/mantle)\\n\\n$0.639825\\n\\n1.20%\\n### [DOT](h\"\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779348899387}}
{"type":"message","id":"ee0bb14b","parentId":"0c2143bd","timestamp":"2026-05-21T07:34:59.387Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_fn4B3NXmCcmgXUPB6IHo4q0f","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Aave Leads DeFi United Recovery After $293M KelpDAO Exploit\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United KelpDAO\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Aave Asks Arbitrum to Unfreeze Stolen Kelp DAO Funds to Contain Fallout\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/arbitrum-dao-asked-to-unfreeze-30k-eth-tied-to-kelp-hacker-direct-them-to-defi-united\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/365431/aave-leads-defi-united-push-to-contain-292m-kelpdao-fallout\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Aave Labs proposed that the Arbitrum DAO unfreeze $73.5 million (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack.\",\n    \"The unfreezing proposal asks for funds to be directed to a remediation effort called 'DeFi United' aimed at restoring rsETH and compensating its holders.\",\n    \"The overall Kelp exploit was valued at approximately $292-$293 million.\",\n    \"Aave was severely impacted by the hack, with its Total Value Locked (TVL) dropping nearly $12 billion in one week.\",\n    \"The hacker used stolen rsETH as collateral on Aave to borrow wrapped Ether, leaving behind over $190 million in bad debt.\",\n    \"Aave founder Stani Kulechov pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money to the recovery efforts.\",\n    \"The 'DeFi United' relief effort has already seen $21 million in contributions from various protocols (including Kelp DAO, BGD Labs, Golem Foundation, Babylon) and individuals.\",\n    \"Another $215 million has been conditionally pledged by Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido, subject to DAO governance votes.\",\n    \"Aave Labs expects the recovery effort to take roughly seven weeks (49 days) to normalize conditions for Arbitrum users and the DeFi ecosystem.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization (DAO) behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack and direct those funds to “DeFi United.” DeFi United is a newly established fund aimed at restoring the backing of Kelp DAO restaked ETH (rsETH) and compensating affected holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council had moved to freeze the 30,765 Ether held in a wallet connected to the massive $292-$293 million Kelp exploit.\\n\\nIn a proposal posted on the Arbitrum governance forum, Aave Labs argued that directing these seized funds to a planned remediation effort would represent a \\\"material contribution\\\" toward restoring normal conditions for Arbitrum users and the wider crypto ecosystem. This submission was made with the active support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi, and Compound. \\n\\nAave was hit particularly hard by the Kelp DAO exploit. Its total value locked (TVL) plummeted by nearly $12 billion in just one week after the hacker put the stolen rsETH tokens up as collateral on Aave’s lending platform to borrow wrapped Ether. This malicious action left Aave with more than $190 million in bad debt and triggered a wave of panic withdrawals.\\n\\nThe initial proposal comes mere days after Aave Labs and others formed the “DeFi United” coalition. According to Dune Analytics data, the initiative has already received about $21 million in active contributions. Notably, Aave's founder, Stani Kulechov, pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money as the DeFi coalition races to contain the fallout. Other initial contributions have come from Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, Golem Foundation, BGD Labs, and the Bitcoin-native DeFi protocol Babylon.\\n\\nBeyond the initial $21 million, another staggering $215 million has been provisionally pledged by major protocols including Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido to assist the recovery effort. These additional funds are currently subject to the approval of their respective governance votes. Additionally, protocols like LayerZero, Ethena, Ink Foundation, and Frax Finance have signaled their intention to provide help.\\n\\nAave Labs specifically asked for the unthawed 30,765 Ether to be sent to a recovery multisig address controlled by Aave, Kelp DAO, and the blockchain security platform Certora. The group stated that even a partial recovery would meaningfully reduce the shortfall. Aave Labs set a timeline for this crisis management effort, expecting the process to unfreeze funds, restore rsETH, and compensate holders to take roughly seven weeks (about 49 days). If the recovery effort falls through for any reason, Aave stated that it would return the unthawed funds.\"\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779348899387}}
{"type":"message","id":"e1cb260e","parentId":"ee0bb14b","timestamp":"2026-05-21T07:34:59.388Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_PO0r8q0sXIPFICfMa90ZV2WR","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Tennessee Bans Bitcoin ATMs\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Tennessee Bitcoin ATM ban\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Tennessee Becomes Second State to Outlaw Bitcoin, Crypto ATMs\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://decrypt.co/365502/tennessee-second-state-outlaw-bitcoin-crypto-atms\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Tennessee is the second U.S. state to outlaw Bitcoin and crypto ATMs.\",\n    \"House Bill 2505 was signed into law by Tennessee Governor Bill Lee on April 13, requiring operators to shut down machines by July 1.\",\n    \"Violations are classified as a Class A misdemeanor.\",\n    \"Federal authorities identified these ATMs as vectors for committing fraud against the elderly.\",\n    \"Americans over 60 lost $257 million to scams involving Bitcoin ATMs last year, a 58% year-over-year increase, according to the FBI.\",\n    \"Indiana was the first state to impose a sweeping ban on Bitcoin ATMs in March.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Tennessee has become the second U.S. state to outlaw Bitcoin ATMs, making it a criminal offense in the Volunteer State to own or operate the machines that federal authorities have identified as a vector committing fraud against the elderly. Whether operators’ kiosks allow customers to purchase Bitcoin or other digital assets with cash, they have until July 1 to pull the plug under House Bill 2505, which Tennessee Governor Bill Lee signed into law on April 13 following the legislation’s introduction earlier this year.\\n\\nThe legislation was co-sponsored by Republican state representatives Cameron Sexton and Jay Reedy. In a March statement, Sexton said the kiosks “have become a gateway for scammers to exploit Tennesseans, especially our seniors.” Sexton noted that victims defrauded while using Bitcoin ATMs often have little hope of recovering their money once it’s gone. That was around the time that local authorities warned of a scam where victims had lost $4 million to overseas scammers posing as law enforcement.\\n\\nReedy, a certified master beef producer, said “Crypto ATMs have given scammers a fast and easy way to target our citizens and scare them into draining their savings.” The two-page bill, which was introduced in February, classifies violations as a Class A misdemeanor, on par in Tennessee with simple drug possession and domestic assault.\\n\\nIn total, Tennessee hosts 651 Bitcoin ATMs, with a majority of them clustered around Nashville, the state’s most populous city and capital, according to Coin ATM Radar. According to FBI numbers released this month, Americans aged over 60 lost $257 million to scams involving Bitcoin ATMs last year, a 58% increase year-over-year. Citizens under 30, for comparison, lost $6.6 million to that type of scam in 2025. In March, Indiana became the first U.S. state to impose a sweeping ban on Bitcoin ATMs. Amid an uptick in scams, several states have passed legislation imposing transaction limits and mandating refunds for victims. In Minnesota, lawmakers are weighing legislation that would follow Tennessee’s lead and ban Bitcoin ATMs across the state.\"\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779348899387}}
{"type":"message","id":"2663f9ec","parentId":"e1cb260e","timestamp":"2026-05-21T07:35:15.312Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_FAZgljOWQiwkivg1Qfh3pFCQ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"./skills/research/README.md","limit":220}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_oFNcVHLCAHs4XALKex2S4Ith","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"./format.py","limit":220}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4KRnmQpeVucnHUlN742ln1qq","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"./research_script.sh","limit":220}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_oNYjPtGvu0IjwqHkLISTVMdN","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"./parse_feeds.py","limit":220}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","usage":{"input":6651,"output":213,"cacheRead":21120,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":27984,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779348899389,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DhsDksM7pyzMfkOG8zkN5JSQBr3El"}}
{"type":"message","id":"8cd18478","parentId":"2663f9ec","timestamp":"2026-05-21T07:35:15.484Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_FAZgljOWQiwkivg1Qfh3pFCQ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research skills — tweet quotes\n\n## `extract_tweet_quotes.py`\n\nFinds `x.com/.../status/...` (and `twitter.com/.../status/...`) URLs inside scraped news text, fetches tweet text via the public FxTwitter API, and outputs **verified** quotes only.\n\n### Quick test (no pipeline)\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/research/extract_tweet_quotes.py \\\n  --text \"Shirzad said https://x.com/faryarshirzad/status/2050325150747484421 in a post.\"\n```\n\nExpect JSON with one object, `\"verified\": true`.\n\n### Test with existing research JSON\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/research/extract_tweet_quotes.py \\\n  --from-file /tmp/research.json \\\n  --field aggregated_raw_content \\\n  --merge-into /tmp/research.json\n```\n\nThen inspect:\n\n```bash\npython3 -c \"import json; d=json.load(open('/tmp/research.json')); print(len(d.get('tweet_quotes',[])), d.get('tweet_quotes',[])[:1])\"\n```\n\n### Full pipeline test\n\n1. Run orchestrator crypto pipeline through Step 1 (research).\n2. Confirm orchestrator logs `TWEET_QUOTES: N verified` (N may be 0 if no x.com links in scrape).\n3. Open `/tmp/research.json` — `tweet_quotes` must be an array; each entry has `url`, `author`, `text`, `verified: true`.\n4. Run writer step; article should include one tweet quote **only if** N ≥ 1.\n\n### Negative test\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/research/extract_tweet_quotes.py \\\n  --text \"No social links here, only https://coindesk.com/article\"\n```\n\nExpect `[]`.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779348915484}}
{"type":"message","id":"eb4e13db","parentId":"8cd18478","timestamp":"2026-05-21T07:35:15.484Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_oFNcVHLCAHs4XALKex2S4Ith","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import json\nimport os\n\nkey_facts = [\n    \"A South Korean court overturned a six-month partial business suspension imposed on Bithumb (CoinDesk).\",\n    \"Judge Gong Hyeon-jin of the Seoul Administrative Court granted the emergency injunction blocking enforcement (Decrypt & CoinDesk).\",\n    \"Bithumb was accused by South Korea's Financial Intelligence Unit of about 6.65 million violations of anti-money laundering rules, including failures to verify customer identities and to block suspicious transactions (CoinDesk & Decrypt).\",\n    \"The initial suspension was accompanied by a $24.6 million fine (CoinDesk).\",\n    \"The court noted that the suspension of core functions like inter-exchange transactions and external transfers would cause difficulty in attracting new customers, particularly as regulatory changes may soon allow listed and professional investment corporations to particulate (Decrypt).\",\n    \"This comes amid broader regulatory scrutiny following a February incident where Bithumb mistakenly credited hundreds of users with 2,000 BTC instead of 2,000 won in a promotion (Decrypt).\"\n]\n\nwith open(\"coindesk_bithumb.txt\", \"r\") as f:\n    coindesk_text = f.read()\n\nwith open(\"decrypt_bithumb.txt\", \"r\") as f:\n    decrypt_text = f.read()\n\nraw_text = coindesk_text + \"\\n\\n\" + decrypt_text\n\noutput = {\n  \"topic_theme\": \"South Korean Court Overturns Bithumb Suspension\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Bithumb suspension lifted\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Bithumb Scores a Legal Win in South Korea as Six-Month Suspension is Lifted by Local Judge\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinDesk\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/01/bithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/366292/south-korean-court-lifts-bithumbs-six-month-business-suspension\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": key_facts,\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": raw_text[:5000] # Ensuring sufficient length\n}\n\nprint(json.dumps(output, indent=2))\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779348915484}}
{"type":"message","id":"ec0c9fc1","parentId":"eb4e13db","timestamp":"2026-05-21T07:35:15.485Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4KRnmQpeVucnHUlN742ln1qq","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/bin/bash\n# Fetch and parse\n# Kelp DAO Exploit / Aave Debt\nurl_cd=$(curl -sL \"https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/\" | grep -A 1 \"Aave raises nearly 80% of the\" | grep \"<link>\" | sed -e 's/<link>//' -e 's/<\\/link>//')\nurl_ct=$(curl -sL \"https://cointelegraph.com/rss\" | grep -A 1 \"Aave asks Arbitrum\" | grep \"<link>\" | sed 's/.*<link><!\\[CDATA\\[//' | sed 's/]]><\\/link>//' | cut -d'?' -f1)\n\n# Fetch article 1\necho \"Fetching Coindesk...\"\ncurl -s \"$url_cd\" -L --max-time 15 | sed 's/<[^>]*>//g' | tr -s ' \\n' | head -c 2000\n\n# Fetch article 2\necho -e \"\\n\\nFetching Cointelegraph...\"\ncurl -s \"$url_ct\" -L --max-time 15 | sed 's/<[^>]*>//g' | tr -s ' \\n' | head -c 2000\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779348915484}}
