### [AVAX](https://decrypt.co/price/avalanche)\\n\\n$9.42\\n\\n2.74%\\n### [HBAR](https://decrypt.co/price/hedera-hashgraph)\\n\\n$0.090681\\n\\n2.00%\\n### [SHIB](https://decrypt.co/price/shiba-inu)\\n\\n$0.00000651\\n\\n6.32%\\n### [USDE](https://decrypt.co/price/ethena-usde)\\n\\n$0.999229\\n\\n0.01%\\n### [SUI](https://decrypt.co/price/sui)\\n\\n$0.936234\\n\\n1.26%\\n### [RAIN](https://decrypt.co/price/rain)\\n\\n$0.00745332\\n\\n1.39%\\n### [PYUSD](https://decrypt.co/price/paypal-usd)\\n\\n$0.999983\\n\\n0.00%\\n### [TON](https://decrypt.co/price/the-open-network)\\n\\n$1.32\\n\\n1.48%\\n### [CRO](https://decrypt.co/price/crypto-com)\\n\\n$0.069339\\n\\n0.09%\\n### [USYC](https://decrypt.co/price/hashnote-usyc)\\n\\n$1.12\\n\\n-0.00%\\n### [XAUT](https://decrypt.co/price/tether-gold)\\n\\n$4,561.39\\n\\n-0.97%\\n### [TAO](https://decrypt.co/price/bittensor)\\n\\n$261.44\\n\\n5.16%\\n### [USDG](https://decrypt.co/price/global-dollar)\\n\\n$0.999782\\n\\n0.00%\\n### [WLFI](https://decrypt.co/price/world-liberty-financial)\\n\\n$0.07344\\n\\n0.47%\\n### [BUIDL](https://decrypt.co/price/blackrock-usd-institutional-digital-liquidity-fund)\\n\\n$1.00\\n\\n0.00%\\n### [PAXG](https://decrypt.co/price/pax-gold)\\n\\n$4,556.28\\n\\n-1.04%\\n### [MNT](https://decrypt.co/price/mantle)\\n\\n$0.639825\\n\\n1.20%\\n### [DOT](h\"\n./final_output.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"Bitcoin Price Correction Risk\",\n./final_output.json:20:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Bitcoin Risks Decline After Futures-Driven April Rally: CryptoQuant\n./result.json:2:  \"topic_theme\": \"U.S. Senate Bans Itself from Using Prediction Markets\",\n./result.json:24:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Acting on a simple, 14-line resolution pushed by Ohio Republican Senator Bernie Moreno, the Senate agreed unanimously to put a restriction between members and the increasingly popular, controversial betting platforms that have drawn scrutiny over insider-trading activity and fights over who has regulatory jurisdiction. “United States Senators have no business engaging in speculative activities like prediction markets while collecting a taxpayer-funded paycheck, period,” said Senator Moreno. The US Senate on Thursday unanimously approved a resolution banning its members and staff, who are often exposed to sensitive information, from using prediction markets. The resolution, passed by unanimous consent, changed the Senate's rules and took immediate effect. “Engaging in any way in a prediction market or trying to place bets where we might have inside information deteriorates the confidence that our constituents have in us,” Republican Senator Bernie Moreno, who introduced the resolution, said on the Senate floor. “By changing the standing rules of the Senate, what we’re doing is allowing our constituents to know, once and for all, that no member of the United States Senate, no member of the staff of the United States Senate, can ever use that inside information as a way to monetize this job whatsoever,” he added. The resolution comes after a special forces soldier involved in the plan to capture former Venezuelan President Nicolás Maduro was charged last week, on April 23, with using classified information to make bets on Polymarket, as lawmakers also air concerns over well-timed bets on the Iran war. Senate Democratic leader Chuck Schumer said on the Senate floor that “of all the issues we debate in Washington, this falls clearly in the category of a ‘no-brainer.’” “We must never allow Congress to turn into a casino where members representing the public can gamble on wars, or economic crises, or elections,” he said. “We should go further; this is a good start, but not enough,” Schumer said. “The administration and its employees must apply these very same rules too, particularly this administration, which shows such a troubling affinity to corruption and self-dealing.” Republican Representative Ashley Hinson posted to X that she would introduce a similar resolution to ban the use of prediction markets in the House. Polymarket posted on X that it fully supported the Senate resolution and its terms of service “already prohibit such conduct, but codifying this into law is a step forward for the industry.” Tarek Mansour, co-founder and CEO of rival prediction market platform Kalshi, also celebrated the resolution in a post on X, adding that it “already proactively blocks members of Congress and enforces against insider trading.”\"\n./crypto_news_summary.json:3:  \"topic_theme\": \"Bitcoin's April Rally Driven by Speculation, Posing Risk of Price Correction\",\n./crypto_news_summary.json:22:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Bitcoin Risks Decline After Futures-Driven April Rally: CryptoQuant\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-decline-rally-speculative-not-structural-cryptoquant\\n\\nPublished Time: Fri, 01 May 2026 10:28:12 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bitcoin risks extended retreat as April rally was futures-driven: CryptoQuant\\n\\nFutures drove up Bitcoin's price in April while spot demand declined, which CryptoQuant warned has historically preceded extended price declines.\\n\\nBitcoin could be setting up for a multimonth price decline, after a rally in April driven mainly by futures traders while spot demand declined, according to the crypto analytics firm CryptoQuant.\\n\\nBitcoin gained around 20% in April, rising from $66,000 to a peak of $79,000 in a rally “driven entirely by growth in perpetual futures demand,” CryptoQuant said in a report on Thursday.\\n\\nMeanwhile, spot demand for Bitcoin contracted throughout the rally, “indicating that the market’s marginal buyer was speculative, not fundamental,” it said.\\n\\n“The divergence between rising price and contracting spot demand is one of the clearest on-chain signals that price gains are speculative rather than structural,” CryptoQuant added.\\n\\nBitcoin is trading around $77,000 at the time of writing, rising 2.1% over the past 24 hours.\\n\\nTitle: Bitcoin Crash Incoming? April Surge Was Built on Shaky Ground, Analysts Warn\\n\\nURL Source: https://decrypt.co/366267/bitcoin-crash-incoming-april-surge-built-shaky-ground-analysts-warn\\n\\nPublished Time: 2026-04-30T20:30:19\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bitcoin Crash Incoming? April Surge Was Built on Shaky Ground, Analysts Warn - Decrypt\\n\\nThe recent surge in Bitcoin’s price, which saw it climb impressively throughout April, may not be as stable as it appears. Market analysts are pointing to underlying data that suggests the rally was built on speculative trading rather than solid, fundamental demand. Experts from analytics firm CryptoQuant have highlighted that the growth was predominantly fueled by perpetual futures contracts, a form of derivative trading that allows for high leverage. Simultaneously, on-chain data shows that actual spot-market buying—the direct purchase of Bitcoin—has been declining. This is a concerning divergence. When prices rise without the backing of genuine buying interest from long-term holders or new retail investors, it often creates a fragile market susceptible to sharp corrections. Historically, such patterns have often been the precursor to significant price drops, as the speculative fervor dies down and the lack of foundational support becomes apparent. While Bitcoin currently holds a strong position near its recent highs, investors are being warned to proceed with caution, as the shaky ground on which the April surge was built could give way, potentially leading to a market-wide crash.\"\n./SOUL.md:86:  \"topic_theme\": \"The core topic (e.g., Bitcoin ETF Inflows Surge)\",\n./SOUL.md:104:  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Combine the raw scraped text from all the articles into one large string...\"\n./SOUL.md:108:**Tweet quotes:** Do not invent tweets in JSON. The orchestrator runs `extract_tweet_quotes.py` on `aggregated_raw_content` to pull verified quotes from `x.com/status/...` links already present in the news articles. You may include `\"tweet_quotes\": []` as a placeholder; the pipeline fills verified entries after your file is written.\n./SOUL.md:112:**File output:** Write the complete JSON to the file path given in your spawn message (e.g. `/tmp/crypto-run-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS/research/raw.json`). Do NOT return the JSON in your chat response. Yield back ONLY \"SUCCESS\".\n./SOUL.md:116:- Ensure the `aggregated_raw_content` is large enough (at least 600 words) to give the Writer plenty of material.\n./SOUL.md:119:- Never fabricate X/Twitter posts or tweet URLs. If articles link to `x.com/.../status/...`, include those URLs in `aggregated_raw_content`; do not make up tweet text.","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779348984337}}
